# Sections system handoff (site-dyvenia)

Branch: `lene/module-based`. Repo: **site-dyvenia** only (TSW is reference, do not copy agency kit fingerprints).

## What shipped

### Composable sections (Nunjucks, not WebC)

- Path: `src/_includes/sections/`
- Types: `hero`, `text`, `highlight`, `list`, `process`, `feature`, `accordion`, `cta`, `posts`, `team`, `form`, `services`, `tabs`, `cases`, `gallery`
- Loop: `_assets.njk` (CSS/JS once) + `_render.njk` (`{% asyncEach %}` + `{% ifAsync %}` + `{% include %}`)
- **Never use macros for section bodies that call async shortcodes** (`{% svg %}`, `{% image %}`) — macros cannot await; hero never closed and everything stacked via `.custom-hero > *`
- Shell helpers in `_shell.njk`: `sectionThemeAttr`, `sectionButtonAttr`, width/align (sync macros OK)
- Layout: `src/_layouts/modular.njk` → include `_loop.njk`
- Co-located CSS: `sections/*.css` → built by `build-css.js` to `src/_includes/css/sections/`
- Modular pages: Solutions + home, about, careers, our-process (`sections[]` + CMS list types). Skip `contact` (TSW Meetings iframe; Dyvenia uses book-a-call links).

### Unified section markup

```
.section-{type}.wrapper[data-section-theme]
  > .full.wrapper.section          ← full-bleed theme paint
    > .section__inner (+ width)    ← content measure only (no bg)
```

Hero/CTA keep media backgrounds; excluded from generic `.section` paint.

### Theme = surface color (not site light/dark)

Site mode stays on `:root` / `data-theme` / `prefers-color-scheme`.

Section themes (`data-section-theme`):
| Value | Role |
|---|---|
| `white` | page white |
| `gray-light` | soft gray band |
| `gray-dark` | dark gray, light text |
| `teal` | soft teal band (was wrongly named blue) |
| `purple` | soft purple band |
| `navy` | dark navy, light text |

Recipes + CTA tokens: `src/assets/css/global/base/themes.css` (imported after `variables.css` in `global.css`).

**Cascade:** section default CTA rules must live in **`blocks` layer** (`button.css`), not `variables` — otherwise base `.button` wins and gray-dark CTAs get light-on-light text.

### Accent / CTA

- `accent: default` (or omit) → theme-fitting CTA via `--section-cta-*`
  - white / gray-light → neutral dark button
  - gray-dark → neutral light button
  - teal / purple → **teal** brand CTA (`#0E909D`)
  - navy → navy CTA
- Override: `neutral` | `teal` | `purple` | `navy`
- No `ghost` in section CMS options (legacy `data-ghost-button` still used elsewhere)

### Color tokens

- `#0E909D` renamed **Teal** (not blue) in `colorsBase.json` → regenerate with `npm run colors`
- Navy is a full vibrant scale + `Navy Dark` standalone
- CSS: `--color-teal*`, `--color-navy-100…900`, `--color-navy-dark`

### Solutions pages

- `src/pages/solutions/*` + `solutions.json` (modular layout, permalink `/solutions/…/`)
- Nav submenu in `src/_data/navigation.yaml`
- CMS: Solutions collection in `admin_content` + `admin_dev`
  - **Do not** add incomplete `filter: { field: title }` — hides all entries
  - Sections list: `collapsed: true`
  - Optional `internal_name` (CMS-only); summary:
    `{{fields.type}}: {{fields.internal_name | default('{{fields.title}}')}}`
    (YAML must use double quotes outside, single quotes inside `default()` or nested `}}` breaks)

### Styleguide

- Multipage under `src/pages/styleguide/` + `styleguide.njk` layout + top nav
- Sections page: live Dyvenia copy from `sectionDemos.js`, neutral `sg-section-doc` bands between demos
- Preview toolbar: theme + accent selects (`styleguide-section-preview.js`) — sets `data-section-theme` only (no inline `--spot-color`)

## Key files

- Sections: `src/_includes/sections/*`
- Themes: `src/assets/css/global/base/themes.css`
- Section paint: `src/assets/css/global/blocks/section.css`
- Buttons/CTA inherit: `src/assets/css/global/blocks/button.css`
- CMS: `src/admin_content/config.yml`, `src/admin_dev/config.yml`
- Tokens: `src/_data/designTokens/colorsBase.json`

